WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.810
<b>Meisei Hospital</b>

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.760
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined.
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.640
<i>Good. No problems with my legs.</i>

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.840
<i>I want to hurry back...</i>

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.520
<i>to that dangerous, magnificent world.</i>

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:52.250
I'm passing back the results 
of your physical fitness exams.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.680
And I'll be passing back your 
quizzes from last week, too.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:56.320
The Strongest
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hRaider

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.160
<i>Tatsuya, are you doing well?</i>

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.640
Mom

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.640
To Tatsuya

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.640
Tatsuya, are you doing well?

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.640
I'll always be rooting for you.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.640
Make sure you work hard in both athletics and studies, okay?

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.030
<i>I'll always be rooting for you.</i>

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.240
Yoigoshi!

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.190
My mom worries too much.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.060
Hang in there.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.570
<i>Make sure you work hard in both 
athletics and studies, okay?</i>

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.410
Yoigoshi-kun!

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:17.420
We heard you're still doing amazing things 
even in a new club! That kabaddi thing.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.030
Your reflexes are so insane 
it's no problem for you, right?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:26.620
No, empty-handed team sport
 isn't as easy as you'd think.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.790
Really... So, kabaddi's a team sport.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.820
How many players do you need for a game?

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.850
How... many?

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:36.540
Huh?

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.760
I don't really know, either.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.240
You'd care, normally, wouldn't you?

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.680
About the number of regulars or 
players on the starting lineup...

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.940
I'm new at this, too, you know?

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.170
Just remembering the rules 
is as much as I can handle.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.820
And I haven't really played many sports.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.850
You must have had sports 
teams in middle school.

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.110
Huh? We didn't have teams.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.010
You didn't have teams?

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.970
Out in the countryside where I lived,
 there weren't many people.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:03.440
The only exercise we could get was 
running on the mountain, or fishing...

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.200
All we could do was challenge nature.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.210
After coming to Tokyo, I could challenge people
 like you and our senpai for the first time.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:14.340
It's been so much fun, I haven't 
had time to give it much thought...

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.030
All right.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.280
I won't ask you any more.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.860
Wha— Why not?

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.890
Didn't I say?

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.390
Usually, games are played seven-on-seven.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.670
Seven players?

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.460
Then we don't have enough people, do we?

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.880
No, as long as we have five people, 
we can have matches.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.360
You just said seven-on-seven!

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.030
I did say "usually," didn't I?

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.360
Think about it.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.330
Up to this point, we were able to play 
one-on-one and two-on-two, weren't we?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:45.900
Even at other schools,

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.660
there are lots of teams that
 don't have many members

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.720
who will have five-on-five games with us.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.860
<i>Why is it all so sloppy?</i>

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:57.420
Kabaddi is a sport where the numbers 
on the court fluctuate anyway.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.480
Fluctuate?

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.000
It's like dodgeball.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.330
Whether on offense or defense,

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.590
players who have a point taken have 
to leave the court. It's a rule.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.100
If their teammates score, they can come back.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.740
Th-Then...

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.700
sometimes the defense will 
have seven players...

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.320
and sometimes there will be only one?

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:16.740
That's right.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:20.480
Though, it doesn't matter much for training,
 so we don't worry about it for practice.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:24.550
These are things that come after 
members know all the rules,

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:28.130
so you only need to think about what 
you can do right now, Yoigoshi.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.970
<i>What I can do right now...</i>

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.940
<i>It's been about a month 
since I started kabaddi.</i>

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.500
<i>I've learned a lot, but what 
is it that's needed to win?</i>

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.510
Good work, guys!

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.380
Date...senpai...

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.220
What?!

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.380
Do you have a minute?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.010
Found it.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.270
Sit Ups 10
Sit and Reach 8
Side Step 6
1500m Run 7
50m Run 6
Standing Long Jump 7
Ball Throw 10

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.270
1500m

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.270
50m

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.270
Standing
Long Jump

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.270
Ball Throw

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.270
Grip Strength

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.270
Sit Ups

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.270
Sit and
Reach

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.930
Those are the results from my fitness test.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.270
Yoigoshi Tatsuya

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.270
<b>Physical Fitness Test
Personal Chart</b>

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.270
Date Shinji

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.270
Noukin High School

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.270
Year 1

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.270
Male

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.270
Kabaddi Team

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.480
I'm lacking in physical strength, in power.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.540
Iura said it, right?

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.020
The number of players on 
the court will fluctuate.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:04.640
If I'm ever on defense alone, I won't 
be able to take down a powerful raider.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.760
So, I'm here asking you 
for ways to get stronger.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.140
Come in for a minute.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:14.380
Baseball?

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.740
I'm from a baseball family.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:20.660
I played from before I can 
remember through middle school.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:22.920
I guess it'd be like you and soccer.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.580
So, I know a lot about how to bulk up, but...

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.610
for kabaddi, your physique is 
already more than good enough.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.270
Don't be stupid. I'm tall, but...

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:39.610
You should put on a little more muscle, 
but you might go over the limit.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:44.780
Name: Date Shinji
Height: 174.2 cm
Blood Type: B
Weight: 79.9 kg

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.970
Eighty kilos.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:44.330
In kabaddi tournaments, 
that's the set weight limit.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.560
Weight limit?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:52.150
For someone over 185cm tall with 
long arms and legs like you,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:58.040
<b>Physical Fitness Test Personal Chart
Noukin High School  Year 1
Kabaddi Team  Male</b>

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:58.040
<b>Name: Yoigoshi Tatsuya
Height: 187.5 cm
Blood Type: A
Weight: 75.2 kg</b>

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.210
even if you get the same 
physical strength as me,

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.790
your sense of balance, which is 
so important in kabaddi, will suffer.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:01.530
And, more than anything else, 
you'll kill that speed you're so proud of.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:06.420
You have power. That's good, and you 
should work on developing it, but...

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.380
It isn't me you should try to be like.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.450
You're unstoppable, right, Yoigoshi?

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.840
Weight limit, huh?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:19.130
<i>I'm only five kilos shy of the limit. 
 I can't afford to put on excess muscle.</i>

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:21.270
<i>Again?</i>

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.610
Mom

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.610
To Tatsuya

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.610
You joined a team?

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.610
Make sure you're respectful toward your senpai,

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.610
and learn as much as you can from them.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.610
<i>You joined a team?</i>

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.570
<i>Make sure you're respectful 
toward your senpai,</i>

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.560
<i>and learn as much as you can from them.</i>

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:31.890
<i>They won't teach me the important stuff.</i>

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.410
We're ready!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:38.970
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.420
<i>Our best raider is Iura,</i>

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:42.420
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:44.420
<i>but his lack of power makes him the only 
one I have a chance of taking down solo.</i>

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.940
He's going off on his own again!

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:51.950
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.260
<i>His expression says he wants 
to take someone, anyone, down.</i>

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.940
<i>But, are you aware?</i>

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:55.240
<i>In kabaddi, the raider has an 
overwhelming advantage one-on-one.</i>

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:55.560
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.000
<i>Where the anti has to tackle,</i>

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.690
<i>the raider only has to touch. 
The difference in difficulty is clear.</i>

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.370
Kabaddi, kabaddi... Kabaddi!

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:06.570
I'm amazed he dodged that!

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.570
<i>What does this guy see?</i>

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:12.280
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.570
Hey, wait! Don't head back!

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:14.310
Huh?

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:19.060
In defense practice, 
you're the only guy I can take down.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:22.330
So you say, but I can't keep up the cant.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.550
I want to get the hang of how a 
tackle feels, in order to win.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:26.680
Yoigoshi.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:30.540
When I told you to think 
about what you can do now,

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:33.800
what I meant was that I wanted you to 
develop the skills you already have.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.810
Skills? On defense, the only thing 
I can do is dodge a touch...

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.380
Can you dodge even at this distance?

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:43.480
Of course I can. Anyone could—

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.480
How do you usually dodge?

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.110
W-Well, I watch my opponent carefully...

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:51.720
and somehow it just sort of happens...

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:52.830
You can't say, can you?

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.260
It's difficult to explain 
an innate talent to others.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:00.030
In your case, Yoigoshi, you have 
an eye for evasion, speed,

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.890
and, most importantly, reach.

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:07.570
That's why you will become Noukin's 
Beast, the strongest raider.

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:10.900
There's no need to push 
yourself on solo defense.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.130
It's on offense where I'm counting 
on you to get us points.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.500
It's not much, but wearing a mask helps 
recreate the breathlessness of the cant.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.850
I'll work up a sweat before practice.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:25.410
My heightened awareness is different 
from that of the ordinary people.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:27.960
Whoa!

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.220
<i>I didn't sense him at all!</i>

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:32.570
Whoops...

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.330
S-Sorry! Are you okay?

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.990
I'm fine.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:37.990
<i>He's so light!</i>

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.630
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:43.080
You're not hurt, are you?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:44.720
Uh, no...

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.480
<i>He's so gaunt, he looks like 
he's on the brink of death.</i>

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.600
That's a relief.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:54.130
<i>Especially compared to the burly types
 I've been hanging out with lately.</i>

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:57.220
Well, I have somewhere to go. 
If you'll excuse me.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:00.640
H-Hold on there!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.770
Uesuna
Park

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:03.880
Here.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:08.190
I'm so sorry. I really am fine.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.650
I'm always like this, so...

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.900
You wobble around like this all the time?

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.760
I am part of a team at my 
high school, a sports team,

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.580
but I just don't seem to get any stronger.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.080
I-I see. A team.

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:25.020
I'm finally going back.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:28.720
Hearing we have an amazing 
new member made me anxious.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.170
I only ran a little and 
I ended up getting dizzy...

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.970
<i>He seems like he's having a rough time.</i>

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:39.220
Our new member is famous in 
a different sport, you see.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.650
<i>Is this a thing where I should
 try to encourage him?</i>

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:46.390
I-I know a guy like that.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.730
He was completely trashed by 
the guys with experience.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.900
Not encouraging

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.590
S-So, I'm sure you'll be fine, right?

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:53.870
Do you think so?

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:57.150
Now that I think about it, 
you were running, too...

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.470
We're getting pretty excited, too, right?

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:58.910
Oh, I was...

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.910
Oh. That's unexpected. It sticks.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.710
What are those guys doing?

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:02.670
Ack!

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:05.030
Yoigoshi's found out about his welcome party!

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:08.420
Man. And we wanted to surprise him—

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:11.170
Hello, sir!

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.220
Huh?

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.410
Oh! Is that Kyohei and Shinji?

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.130
Welcome back, Captain!

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.280
C-Captain?!

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:21.850
<b>Noukin High School Third-Year Kabaddi Team Captain
Ojo Masato</b>

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.850
Yoigoshi! Why are you with him?

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.060
Yo....

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.510
Yoigoshi-kun?!

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.420
What's going on?

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:32.230
<i>This is the team leader?</i>

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.410
<i>The leader that manages these musclebound 
morons and that fiendish four-eyes?</i>

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.540
<i>I don't understand. 
How could a guy like this...</i>

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.370
Welcome back!

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:41.620
Thank you for your hard work
 in fulfilling your obligations!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:42.660
Was he serving time?

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.620
It's been a while, hasn't it, Soma?

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.330
You've met each other?

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.220
Last winter.

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:51.910
Cap is the one who scouted Azemichi.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.720
Why is that guy the captain?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:55.640
Why do you ask?

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.340
I mean, he seems really weak...

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.800
What can he do with a body like that?

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:06.050
Ask him yourself. This is the 
perfect chance, isn't it?

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:08.560
Cheers!

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.560
Let's play cards, Captain!

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.570
But not with Iura-san.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.570
Why?

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:16.070
Because you never lose, Iura-san.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.910
I'm not very good at cards.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.450
<i>So, he's not super smart 
or anything either, huh?</i>

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:23.890
Yoigoshi-kun, you should come play, too!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.720
I'm fine. Once we start a game, 
there'll be no end to it.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.300
This guy really, really hates losing.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.540
It's one thing if it's only a test of abilities,

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:37.510
but when luck is involved,
 he'll just keep playing until he wins.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:38.840
Really?

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:42.050
If it's a test of abilities, 
there's one I want to try!

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.160
Arm wrestling!

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:46.750
In that case, we'll leave 
Date and Misumi out.

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:48.810
Uh oh. He's holding a grudge about earlier.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.410
And he dragged me into it, too.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:01.610
Though imperfect... being captain allows 
you to begin to see many things.

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.800
Like how the team looks up to me,

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:05.880
or conversely, a wariness...

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:08.370
like when my worth is being tested.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:12.710
I heard that "Yoigoshi the Unstoppable"
 had grown to hate sports...

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.880
Seeing you so serious 
about this makes me happy.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:20.730
So, I'll show you a little 
of why I'm captain.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:25.640
Well, then. Ready...

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:26.590
Go!

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:28.770
Huh?

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:30.640
Captain!

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:34.020
The captain has only just been discharged 
from the hospital, Yoigoshi!

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:38.230
<i>There was no weight to him. 
I couldn't feel any power at all!</i>

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:41.030
<i>Has my own strength drastically improved?</i>

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:42.570
Azemichi!

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.580
<i>Th-That doesn't seem to be the case.</i>

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:55.170
<i>He's at a level where he 
can compete with Iura?</i>

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.490
Darn it.

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:59.750
Hey. This is too much work, 
so I'm just going to ask flat-out.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.580
Why are you the captain?

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:04.420
You're clearly weak, and you can't 
possibly be cut out for kabaddi.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:06.050
Hey, Yoigoshi!

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:09.860
That's true. My body isn't 
really built for kabaddi.

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:12.130
But the reason I'm captain...

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.680
is because I'm the strongest.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:17.690
<i>What?</i>

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:24.030
Even if I try to stop you, 
you won't listen, right?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.890
Yeah. I'll only do a little.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:27.840
Don't get reckless.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.790
After those arm wrestling results, 
he's gonna do kabaddi?

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.620
They say you're fast on your feet, right?

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.340
A fast rookie playing 
the same position as me.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.420
It'd make you anxious, right?

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:41.920
There hasn't been 
anyone like that up to now.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:46.680
I've been so anxious to play...

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.930
So, it wasn't that you were freaking out?

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.480
Let's hurry up and play a game, okay?

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:54.680
Hurry up...

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:56.450
Let's do this!

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.070
No, no.

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:04.860
Cap, I don't want you to strain yourself.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.450
Will you be able to do introductions 
in a one-turn game?

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:08.330
Yes.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.950
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.930
I'm a raider, so would 
someone play defense for me?

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.150
Of course, I'll be the one doing it.

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:23.130
I'm curious to see what 
you can do, after all.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.380
I want to, too!

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.880
Thank you. Anyone else?

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.630
We're not wearing clothes 
we can move in, so...

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:32.260
I'll referee, so please 
go ahead with two-on-one.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.230
<i>What's with them?</i>

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:36.130
<i>They're not interested 
in the challenge at all?</i>

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.770
<i>Well, he is just out of the hospital...</i>

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.320
<i>and with such a slender build...</i>

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:45.360
You were saying something about being 
the strongest, but I don't believe you.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.360
I've got reach and speed.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:50.360
<b>Defense
First-Years</b>

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:49.460
And this guy's little, but he's got power.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.870
<b>Raider
Ojo Masato</b>

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:53.870
Does it look like I have nothing?

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:57.120
For now... Let's give it a try.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.750
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:01.750
<i>I don't sense anything.</i>

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.220
<i>He's "scentless."</i>

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:07.990
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:08.380
<i>People who possess something exceptional 
have a particular air to them, a scent.</i>

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.950
<i>There isn't anything at 
all emanating from this guy.</i>

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:16.600
Kabaddi.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.390
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:22.770
Kabaddi.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.760
<i>Huh? Just now...</i>

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.130
<i>Did he touch me?</i>

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.620
W-Wait! That one didn't count!

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.330
I let my guard down! Let's go one more time!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.680
I thought so.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:37.570
Kei! Can we go again?

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:38.910
I suppose you'll have to.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:40.030
Yay!

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:43.880
So, the captain's skill 
works on you, too, Yoigoshi?

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:44.760
Skill?

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:48.680
I first met the captain 
when I was fishing, and...

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.960
No good, huh?

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:00.650
Wow!

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.400
Fishing in the winter is really hard.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.480
I asked how he caught so many.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:09.340
He said, "Offset your 
breathing and your timing."

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:12.700
"If you do that, living things 
won't be able to react."

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.360
Am I some kind of fish?

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.180
The reality is, you weren't 
able to do anything, right?

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:20.330
I wasn't on my guard earlier.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.540
Then, this time, let's get serious.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:29.090
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.090
<i>This time, I'll watch closely.</i>

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:32.830
<i>A low stance, balanced for 
both attack and evasion...</i>

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:36.520
<i>A smooth, difficult to read, steady cant.</i>

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:42.370
<i>And he's very likely keeping me and 
Azemichi at the edges of his vision.</i>

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:43.820
<i>An obscure line of sight.</i>

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.600
<i>Huh?</i>

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:48.480
<i>That means I don't know 
anything about anything.</i>

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:49.610
Kabaddi.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.200
Kabaddi!

00:16:58.510 --> 00:16:59.590
<i>From the side?</i>

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:01.490
<i>I thought he was in front of me!</i>

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:03.680
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:05.000
He's pursuing hard!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.500
Leave it to me!

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.590
<i>He didn't come in?!</i>

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.180
Kabaddi.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.260
<i>No way. I thought I was in his blind spot.</i>

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:19.900
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:19.510
<i>He read us completely.</i>

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:24.640
It isn't just speed, is it?

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:26.900
When I think you won't come, you do.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:28.910
When I think you're coming, you don't.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:31.270
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:30.780
Is your specialty the feint?

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:33.630
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:35.920
I'm doing the cant right now...

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:35.920
I'm doing the cant right now...

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.920
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.820
You can stop your cant!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:37.030
The next one will be the real one.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:41.790
Asking a question in the middle 
of a match. That's interesting.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.300
But you're a little off.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:46.110
My skill isn't quite as civilized as a feint.

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:48.170
I won't tell you any more yet.

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.730
Well, that's petty of you.

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:51.520
Then, how about my next question?

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:52.300
Hm?

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:55.580
If I can stop you, 
would you say I'm strong?

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:01.260
Yes. Undoubtedly so.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.800
<i>He's starting to sense something.</i>

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:05.950
<i>That's Yoigoshi for you. 
His instincts are good.</i>

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:08.770
Okay. This time really is the last time.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.020
Sir!

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:15.910
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:15.910
<i>Under normal circumstances, 
human movement is mostly predictable.</i>

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:20.280
<i>The placement of the center of gravity, 
areas of tension, line of sight.</i>

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:20.280
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:26.750
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:23.240
<i>But I don't feel anything from this guy.</i>

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.000
<i>If I can't read him, then all I can 
do is use my reflexes to evade...</i>

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:28.980
<i>so that I can't be read either...</i>

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:30.040
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.040
<i>Just like him...</i>

00:18:30.550 --> 00:18:31.790
Kabaddi...

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:38.550
Kabaddi.

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.720
<i>He's copying the captain?!</i>

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:44.760
Kabaddi.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.420
Blast! I let him get away!

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:50.080
Yoigoshi! What did you just do?

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.360
Huh? Nothing. I just spaced out!

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.100
You're kidding me. What was that?

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:55.360
I don't know.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.380
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:58.380 --> 00:18:59.360
Kabaddi...

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:03.010
<i>The unconscious copying of a 
man who excels at learning.</i>

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:06.490
<i>The "scent of the exceptional" 
they had spoken of began to rise.</i>

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:11.600
<i>However, there was one more 
beast giving off that scent.</i>

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:15.670
Kabaddi!

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:19.980
<i>Is he angry? No... He's smiling.</i>

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.520
<i>Either way, this scent...</i>

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:27.560
Kabaddi.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:31.240
<i>Clear motions of attack! It's a feint.</i>

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.030
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.060
<i>It wasn't! It was just what it looked like!</i>

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:36.110
Kabaddi...

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:40.070
<i>I can't anticipate him! His movements 
are totally different from before!</i>

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:46.220
<i>In general, the raider's arm 
is unsuitable for a take down.</i>

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:47.890
<i>Impulsively grabbing it means</i>

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:50.350
<i>you either believe you can 
win through strength,</i>

00:19:50.350 --> 00:19:52.740
<i>or that you are, quite simply, afraid.</i>

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:01.050
<i>Why...</i>

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.240
<i>Why am I on the ground?</i>

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.470
<i>Was I taken down? By him?</i>

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.450
Kabaddi...

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:16.400
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:23.100
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:23.940
He made it back!

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.910
Yay! Two points!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:37.450
This really is fun.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:38.810
Too much fun.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:42.200
You completely switched on 
at the end there, didn't you?

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.590
You'll hurt yourself again.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:47.400
That was the first time 
anyone has ever copied me.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:48.550
I was just so happy.

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:50.640
Copying you wasn't something 
I did out of logic.

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:53.770
More importantly, how did 
you take me down at the end?

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.050
It was a type of counter.

00:20:56.050 --> 00:20:58.250
It's used in boxing and stuff.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:20:59.650
A counter?

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:01.840
Even though I hadn't attacked?

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:04.760
Even so, you breathe, don't you?

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:06.660
Sudden actions...

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:11.400
When people go to use their strength, 
they always either stop breathing or exhale.

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:16.430
Thinking about it in reverse, when you 
inhale, you are very nearly unguarded.

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:19.310
If I match my max to that moment,

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:21.590
both touching and tackling become simple.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.590
I'm not good in a 
"ready, go" situation, though.

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.440
<i>I couldn't sense anything from this guy.</i>

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:31.410
<i>He didn't let me sense anything, 
and then, a counter...</i>

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:33.420
<i>No wonder he's a pain to deal with.</i>

00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:35.350
<i>On top of that, this guy is...</i>

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:39.610
<i>still hiding something from me!</i>

00:21:41.470 --> 00:21:44.860
Our captain's been playing kabaddi 
as a raider for over ten years!

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:45.860
Ten years?

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:49.700
You little... How could you tell me 
to go be "the strongest raider"?!

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.240
What's this? Yoigoshi, are you giving up?

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:55.990
Don't be stupid.

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.460
I've only just seen the way ahead.

00:21:58.670 --> 00:21:59.700
I'll do it.

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:02.480
Oh, that's right!

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:05.690
Yoigoshi-kun, there's something 
important I forgot to tell you.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:10.640
My name. Now that I think about it, 
I haven't told you yet, have I?

00:22:12.340 --> 00:22:13.600
It's fine.

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:14.480
Huh?

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:17.980
I can just call you "Captain," right?

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"The Match Begins!!!"</b>

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:52.560
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.560
Next time, "The Match Begins!!!"

00:23:52.560 --> 00:23:53.340
Kabaddi!
